can-calc-bit-timing: replace QNX's min()/max() macros.

QNX's <stdlib.h> defines untyped min()/max() macros; compat.h then
redefines them (with its type-checked versions), which GCC warns about.
#undef them first so compat.h's definitions are the ones in effect, as on
Linux.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/calc-bit-timing/compat.h
+++ b/calc-bit-timing/compat.h
@@ -52,7 +52,11 @@ typedef __u32 u32;
  * min()/max()/clamp() macros that also do
  * strict type-checking.. See the
  * "unnecessary" pointer comparison.
+ *
+ * QNX's <stdlib.h> defines its own (untyped) min()/max(): replace them.
  */
+#undef min
+#undef max
 #define min(x, y) ({				\
 	typeof(x) _min1 = (x);			\
 	typeof(y) _min2 = (y);			\
